 00\nAir Outlets and Inlets\n23 82 00\nConvection Heating and Cooling Units\nDIVISION 26 - ELECTRICAL\n26 05 00\nGeneral Electrical Requirements\n26 05 19\nLow-Voltage Electrical Power Conductors and Cables\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nTable of Contents - 2\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nTABLE OF CONTENTS\n26 05 20\n26 05 26\n26 05 29\n26 05 33\n26 05 53\n26 27 16\n26 27 26\n26 28 13\n26 28 16.16\n26 28 26\n26 51 00\n\nMineral-Insulated Metal-Sheathed Cable\nGrounding and Bonding for Electrical Systems\nHangers and Supports for Electrical Systems\nRaceway and Boxes for Electrical Systems\nIdentification for Electrical Systems\nElectrical Cabinets and Enclosures\nWiring Devices\nFuses\nEnclosed Switches\nEnclosed Transfer Switches\nInterior Lighting\n\nDIVISION 28 – ELECTRONIC SAFETY AND SECURITY\n28 31 00\nFire Detection and Alarm\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nTable of Contents - 3\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19\n\nSECTION 02 41 19 - SELECTIVE DEMOLITION\nPART 1\n1.1\n\nRELATED DOCUMENTS\nA.\n\n1.2\n\n1.4\n\n1.5\n\nThe following documents apply to all required work for the Project: (1) the Contract Drawings, (2) the\nSpecifications, (3) the General Conditions, (4) the Addendum and (5) the Contract (the Owner’s\nStandard Construction Contract).\n\nSUMMARY\nA.\n\n1.3\n\n- GENERAL\n\nSection Includes:\n1.\nDemolition and removal of selected portions of building or structure.\n2.\nDemolition and removal of selected site elements.\n\nDEFINITIONS\nA.\n\nRemove: Detach items from existing construction and legally dispose of them off-site unless indicated\nto be removed and salvaged or removed and reinstalled.\n\nB.\n\nRemove and Salvage: Carefully detach from existing construction, in a manner to prevent damage, and\nmake ready for reuse.\n\nC.\n\nRemove and Reinstall: Detach items from existing construction, prepare for reuse, and reinstall where\nindicated.\n\nD.\n\nExisting to Remain: Existing items of construction that are not to be permanently removed and that are\nnot otherwise indicated to be removed, removed and salvaged, or removed and reinstalled.\n\nMATERIALS OWNERSHIP\nA.\n\nUnless otherwise indicated, demolition waste becomes property of the Contractor.\n\nB.\n\nHistoric items, relics, antiques, and similar objects including, but not limited to, cornerstones and their\ncontents, commemorative plaques and tablets, and other items of interest or value to the Owner that\nmay be uncovered during demolition remain the property of the Owner.\n1.\nCarefully salvage in a manner to prevent damage and promptly return to the Owner.\n\nPREINSTALLATION MEETINGS\nA.\n\nPredemolition Conference: Conduct conference at Project site.\n1.\nInspect and discuss the condition of construction to be selectively demolished.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19 - 1\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents\nApril 12, 2024\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19\n\n2.\n3.\n4.\n5.\n1.6\n\nSUBMITTAL PROCEDURES\nA.\n\n1.7\n\n1.8\n\n1.9\n\nReview structural load limitations of the existing structure.\nReview and finalize selective demolition schedule and verify availability of materials,\ndemolition personnel, equipment, and facilities needed to make progress and avoid delays.\nReview requirements of work performed by other trades that rely on substrates exposed by\nselective demolition operations.\nReview areas where existing construction is to remain and requires protection.\n\nRefer to the “Information for Bidders BID Agreement and General Conditions Governing All Contracts\nfor Construction” for further information.\n\nSUBMITTALS\nA.\n\nProposed Protection Measures: Submit a report, including drawings, that indicates the measures\nproposed for protecting individuals and property including protection for environmental protection, for\ndust control, and for noise control. Indicate proposed locations and construction of barriers.\n\nB.\n\nSchedule of Selective Demolition Activities: Indicate the following:\n1.\nDetailed sequence of selective demolition and removal work, with starting and ending dates\nfor each activity. Ensure the Owner's on-site operations are uninterrupted.\n2.\nInterruption of utility services. Indicate how long utility services will be interrupted.\n3.\nCoordination for shutoff, capping, and continuation of utility services.\n4.\nUse of elevator and stairs.\n5.\nCoordination of the Owner’s continuing occupancy of portions of the existing building and of\nthe Owner's partial occupancy of completed Work.\n\nC.\n\nInventory: Submit a list of items to be removed and salvaged and deliver to the Owner prior to the start\nof demolition.\n\nD.\n\nPredemolition Photographs or Video: Submit before Work begins.\n1.\nWarranties: Documentation indicated that existing warranties are still in effect after the\ncompletion of selective demolition.\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\nA.\n\nInventory: Submit a list of items that have been removed and salvaged.\n\nB.\n\nLandfill Records: Indicate receipt and acceptance of hazardous wastes by a landfill facility licensed to\naccept hazardous wastes.\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19 - 2\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents\nApril 12, 2024\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19\n\nA.\n1.10\n\n1.11\n\nFIELD CONDITIONS\nA.\n\nThe Owner will occupy portions of the building immediately adjacent and in the selective demolition\narea. Conduct selective demolition so the Owner’s operations will not be disrupted.\n\nB.\n\nConditions existing at the time of inspection for bidding purposes will be maintained by the Owner as\nfar as practical.\n\nC.\n\nNotify the Owner of discrepancies between existing conditions and Drawings before proceeding with\nselective demolition.\n\nD.\n\nHazardous Materials:\n1.\nIf suspected hazardous materials are encountered, do not disturb; immediately notify the\nOwner.\n2.\nDo not disturb hazardous materials or items suspected of containing hazardous materials except\nunder procedures specified elsewhere in the Contract Documents.\n\nE.\n\nStorage or sale of removed items or materials on-site is not permitted.\n1.\nUtility Service: Maintain existing utilities indicated to remain in service and protect them\nagainst damage during selective demolition operations.\n2.\nMaintain fire-protection facilities in service during selective demolition operations.\n\nWARRANTY\nA.\n\nExisting Warranties: Remove, replace, patch, and restore materials and surfaces cut or damaged during\nselective demolition, by methods and with materials so as not to void existing warranties. Notify\nwarrantor before proceeding. Existing warranties include the following:\n1.\nExisting roof system.\n\nB.\n\nNotify warrantor on completion of selective demolition, and obtain documentation verifying that\nexisting system has been inspected and warranty remains in effect. Submit documentation at Project\ncloseout.\n\nPART 2\n2.1\n\nRefer to “Information for Bidders BID Agreement and General Conditions Governing All Contracts\nfor Construction.”\n\n- PRODUCTS\n\nPERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS\nA.\n\nRegulatory Requirements: Comply with governing EPA notification regulations before beginning\nselective demolition. Comply with hauling and disposal regulations of ACM (asbestos containing\nmaterial).\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19 - 3\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents\nApril 12, 2024\n\nSelective Demolition\n02 41 19\n\nB.\nPART 3\n3.1\n\n3.3\n\n- EXECUTION\n\nEXECUTION REQUIREMENTS\nA.\n\n3.2\n\nStandards: Comply with ANSI/ASSE A10.6 and NFPA 241.\n\nRefer to the Owner's General Conditions for execution requirements.\n\nEXAMINATION\nA.\n\nVerify that utilities have been disconnected and capped before starting selective demolition operations.\n\nB.\n\nSurvey existing conditions and correlate with requirements indicated to determine extent of selective\ndemolition required.\n\nC.\n\nWhen unanticipated mechanical, electrical, or structural elements that conflict with intended function\nor design are encountered, investigate and measure the nature and extent of conflict. Promptly submit\na written report to the Owner.\n\nD.\n\nEngage a Professional Engineer licensed in the State of New York to perform an engineering survey of\ncondition of building to determine whether removing any element might result in structural deficiency\nor unplanned collapse of any portion of the structure or adjacent structures during selective building\ndemolition operations.\n1.\nPerform surveys as the Work progresses to detect hazards resulting from selective demolition\nactivities.\n2.\nSurvey of Existing Conditions: Record existing conditions by use of measured drawings and\npreconstruction photographs.\n3.\nInventory and record the condition of items to be removed and salvaged. Provide photographs\nof conditions that might be misconstrued as damage caused by salvage operations.\n4.\nBefore selective demolition or removal of existing building elements that will be reproduced\nor duplicated in final Work, make a permanent record of measurements, materials, and\nconstruction details required to make exact reproduction.\n\nMECHANICAL/ELECTRICAL SYSTEMS","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138591976}}
{"type":"message","id":"43a000f7","parentId":"cd4271ef","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:56.913Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01VHqugPmPf9bW39BCVWFj3z","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"-NO TEXT THIS PAGE-\n\n-NO TEXT THIS PAGE-\n\nWORK TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\nDO YOU ANTICIPATE SUBCONTRACTING ANY PORTION OF THE WORK ON THIS PROJECT?\nYES\n\nNO\n\nIf yes, please indicate below, each activity you are proposing to subcontract and its appropriate dollar value.\nWork to be Subcontracted:\n\nTOTAL AMOUNT TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\n\nApproximate $ Value:\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n\n____________________________________\n\n___________________________\n\nContractor’s Signature\n\nDate\n\nBid Form B-1\n20\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\nSAVE\n\nCLEAR\n\nHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nM/WBE Utilization Plan\nInstructions - In the area below, please provide the business full legal name, such as \"ABC Company, Inc.\" or \"ABC Firm, LLC\". Please also provide the contact\ninformation of the person responsible for the compliance and reporting functions under this agreement.\nSolicitation Name\n\nSolicitation M/WBE Goal\n\nVendor Full Legal Name\n\nVendor Tax ID#\n\nAddress\n\nTelephone #\n\nVendor M/WBE Compliance Contact Name\n\nEmail\n\n%\n\nInstructions - In the table below, briefly describe the scope of work for each M/WBE subcontractor, such as \"Electrical work\", \"Training\", \"Furniture\". List the percentage\nof the scope of work against the total estimated value of the contract. For example, if this is a three year contract worth $100 a year, and the subcontractor's work is a\ntotal of $90 over the three years, the percent would be equal to $90/($100 * 3 years) or 30%. Note M/WBE vendors must be certified by New York State or New York\nCity to qualify. If additional space is needed please use table provided on page 2.\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\nPlease ensure combined M/WBE Goal calculated below meets or exceeds the solicitation M/WBE goal. If through good faith efforts, the solicitation M/WBE Goal\ncannot be met, please complete the Waiver Request Form. \t\t\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\n% of\n\nCertification\nType\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\nCombined M/WBE utilization goal (sum of percentages)\n\n0 %\n\nSubmission of this form constitutes the vendor’s acknowledgement and agreement to comply with the M/WBE requirements set forth as part of the solicitation. Failure to provide complete and\naccurate information may result in a rejection of the bid/proposal, and noncompliance with the goals may result in termination of the resulting contract, monetary damages, and debarment.\n\nPrepared By (Signature)\nName (Print)\n\nTelephone no.\n\nTitle of Preparer (Print)\n\nEmail address\nJOC INFORMATION FOR BIDDERS AS OF APRIL 2022\n\nPage 20A\n\nHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nAdditional NYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\n\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\nCertification\nType\n\n% of\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n\nJOC INFORMATION FOR BIDDERS AS OF APRIL 2022\n\nPage 20B\n\nACKNOWLEDGMENT\nName of Bidder: ___________________________________________________________\nBidder is Individual ( ) Partnership ( ) Corporation ( ) Joint Venture"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":4928,"aggregated":"-NO TEXT THIS PAGE-\n\n-NO TEXT THIS PAGE-\n\nWORK TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\nDO YOU ANTICIPATE SUBCONTRACTING ANY PORTION OF THE WORK ON THIS PROJECT?\nYES\n\nNO\n\nIf yes, please indicate below, each activity you are proposing to subcontract and its appropriate dollar value.\nWork to be Subcontracted:\n\nTOTAL AMOUNT TO BE SUBCONTRACTED\n\nApproximate $ Value:\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n$\n\n____________________________________\n\n___________________________\n\nContractor’s Signature\n\nDate\n\nBid Form B-1\n20\nINFORMAITON FOR BIDDERS\n\nSAVE\n\nCLEAR\n\nHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nM/WBE Utilization Plan\nInstructions - In the area below, please provide the business full legal name, such as \"ABC Company, Inc.\" or \"ABC Firm, LLC\". Please also provide the contact\ninformation of the person responsible for the compliance and reporting functions under this agreement.\nSolicitation Name\n\nSolicitation M/WBE Goal\n\nVendor Full Legal Name\n\nVendor Tax ID#\n\nAddress\n\nTelephone #\n\nVendor M/WBE Compliance Contact Name\n\nEmail\n\n%\n\nInstructions - In the table below, briefly describe the scope of work for each M/WBE subcontractor, such as \"Electrical work\", \"Training\", \"Furniture\". List the percentage\nof the scope of work against the total estimated value of the contract. For example, if this is a three year contract worth $100 a year, and the subcontractor's work is a\ntotal of $90 over the three years, the percent would be equal to $90/($100 * 3 years) or 30%. Note M/WBE vendors must be certified by New York State or New York\nCity to qualify. If additional space is needed please use table provided on page 2.\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\nPlease ensure combined M/WBE Goal calculated below meets or exceeds the solicitation M/WBE goal. If through good faith efforts, the solicitation M/WBE Goal\ncannot be met, please complete the Waiver Request Form. \t\t\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\n% of\n\nCertification\nType\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\nCombined M/WBE utilization goal (sum of percentages)\n\n0 %\n\nSubmission of this form constitutes the vendor’s acknowledgement and agreement to comply with the M/WBE requirements set forth as part of the solicitation. Failure to provide complete and\naccurate information may result in a rejection of the bid/proposal, and noncompliance with the goals may result in termination of the resulting contract, monetary damages, and debarment.\n\nPrepared By (Signature)\nName (Print)\n\nTelephone no.\n\nTitle of Preparer (Print)\n\nEmail address\nJOC INFORMATION FOR BIDDERS AS OF APRIL 2022\n\nPage 20A\n\nHHC-100HHC\nREV. 11/2021\n\nAdditional NYS/NYC Certified M/WBE Subcontractors/Suppliers\n\nNYS/NYC Certified M/WBE\nSubcontractors/Suppliers\nFull Legal Name\n\nSub\nPoint Of Contact\n\nSub\nEmail\n\nSub\nTelephone\n\nSub\nTax ID\n\nCertification\nType\n\n% of\n\nScopes of Work\n\nSubcontracts/\n\nsupplies/\nservices\n\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n%\n\nJOC INFORMATION FOR BIDDERS AS OF APRIL 2022\n\nPage 20B\n\nACKNOWLEDGMENT\nName of Bidder: ___________________________________________________________\nBidder is Individual ( ) Partnership ( ) Corporation ( ) Joint Venture","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138596904}}
{"type":"message","id":"5a011e74","parentId":"43a000f7","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:09:57.122Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01EHFdYSDMRmdt5LMy8RMSab","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"READ CAREFULLY\n\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor\nNew York, NY 10041\n\nSECTION “A “\nBIDDING OFFICE: CONTRACT SERVICES\nPROJECT TITLE:\n\n1120220: Fire Pump & Standpipe\nReplacement at Bellevue Hospital Center\n370 CCDs\n\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF\nTHE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR LAW AGREEMENT\n\nNOTICE: ALL BIDDERS MUST REFER TO THE CONTENTS OF THE\nATTACHED BID PACKAGE FOR BIDDER REQUIREMENTS\n\nREAD CAREFULLY\nNEW YORK CITY HEALTH AND HOSPITAL CORPORATION\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nSECTION A\nBID FORMS\nCONSTRUCTIONS CONTRACTS\nUSE THESE BID FORMS ONLY, NOT THOSE IN THE BOOK\nTO ALL BIDDERS:\nALL BIDS SUBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC H+H (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR THAT IS AWARED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER\nOF ASSENT AND SUBMIT IT TO NYC H+H\nYou must submit a completed Bid Proposal (Bid Form A‐1, Page 15) and a completed Bid Bond with your Bid.\nFailure to submit a completed Bid Proposal and a completed Bid Bond with your bid and failure to meet the\nterms of the HHC PROJECT LABOR AGREEMENT shall cause your bid to be declared non‐responsive. Failure to\ncomplete and submit all other items in Section “A” may cause you bid to be declared non‐response. Refer to\nthe enclosed checklist when preparing your bid proposal. Your bid proposal will be checked for responsiveness\nfrom this checklist.\nEVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED. IF ITEMS DO NOT APPLY, INSERT N/A. DO NOT LEAVE BLANK SPACES.\n\nSECTION “A” IS AS FOLLOWS\n CONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST – PAGE 1A\n BID FORM A‐1,\nPAGE 1\n BID BREAKDOWN:\nPAGE 1 OF 3\n BID FORM A‐1‐1\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\n BID FORM A‐1‐2\nINSURANCE INFORMATION\n BID FORMS A‐2\nPAGES 16‐19 (BID BOND IS REQUIRED FOR ALL BIDS OF $50,000 OR MORE)\n WORK EXPERIENCE\nATTACHMENTS AE‐1 – AE‐4\n VENDEX QUESTIONNAIRES (VENDOR ENTITY AND PRINCIPLE QUESTIONNAIRES) FOR ALL BIDS OF\n$100,000 OR MORE. PLEASE USE LINK (https://passport.cityofnewyork.us)\n\nNOTICE\nALL BIDDERS MUST BE ABLE TO SUBSTANTIATE THAT THEY COMPLETED CONTRACT(S) OF SIMILAR SCOPE\nWITH THE PAST FIVE (5) YEARS.\n\nTECHNICAL QUESTIONS MUST BE SUBMITTED IN WRITING NO LATER THAN (DATE IS PROVIDED)\n\nCONSTRUCTION BID CHECKLIST\n1. Bid Form A‐1, Bidders Proposal – (page 15)\nTrades, Licensee Name, License Number, License Expiration Date\nAddenda Number (if applicable)\nTotal Lump Sum Bid Price in numbers and Words\nBidder’s company Name/Phone No./Fax No.\nN.Y.S Certified MBE/WBE\nBidder’s Signature and Date\nBidder’s Corporate Seal (if applicable)\n2. Bid Alternate(s) (if applicable)\n\nFILLED IN\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n( )\n\nAll Blanks for Dollar Amounts\nIndicate Whether Amount(s) are Additions or Deductions\n\n( )\n( )\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\nBID FORM A‐1‐2\n\n( )\n( )\n\n3. Bid form A‐2\n\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO 220 AND 230\nINSURANCE CERTIFICATES\n10% Bid Bond – (page 16)\n\n( )\n\nPrincipal’s Name\nSurety Company’s Name\nDollar Amount in Words and Numbers\nProposed Contract (description) (pages 18 & 19)\nPrincipal Signed, Sealed and Notarized\nSurety Signed, Sealed and Notarized\n4. Bid Breakdown\nBidder’s Name and Date\nLocation of Facility, Project No. and Project Title\nItems No. and Item of Work\nColumns 1‐5\nNo. 6 – Total Bid Price\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n5. Completed Contracts – (pages AE‐1 – AE‐4\nContractor/Subcontractor\nFacility/Project Name/Address\nOwner/Project Manager/Phone No.\nSurety Company/Agent/ Phone No.\nBonding Amount\nContract Award Amount/Contract No.\nAll Dates\nConstruction Manager/Architect/Address/Reference/Phone No.\n\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n(\n\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n)\n\n6. Vendex\n\n( )\n\n( )\n\nOffice of Facilities Development, Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442-3680 | Fax: (212) 442-3741\nBID PROPOSAL FOR CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS\nTRADE:\n\nPROJECT ID:\n\nPROJECT DESCRIPTION:\nALL BIDS USBMITTED SHALL BE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE TERMS OF THE NYC HEALTH + HOSPITAL (HHC) PROJECT LABOR\nAGREEMENT. EACH CONTRACTOR AWARDED A CONTRACT SHALL BE REQUIRED TO EXECUTE A LETTER OF ASSENT AND SUBMIT\nIT TO NYC H+H.\n*LICENSEE: ______________________ LINCENSE NO. __________________ EXPIRATION DATE: ____________\nThe bidder confirms that its bid for the above project includes all work in accordance with the Contract Documents and Addenda.\nAll Addenda must contain the signature of the principal or authorized representative, and the date, and must be submitted with\nthe bid proposal as part of Section “A”. The bidder is to list all said addenda by number as follows:\nAddenda: ____________________ (LIST AND INCLUDE ALL ADDENDA IN BID PACKAGE)\nBASE BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\nTOTAL BID PRICE: _________________________________________________________________________\n(In Words)\n1. BASE BID PRICE\n$\n2. ALTERNATE # 1 PRICE\n$\n3. ALTERNATE # 2 PRICE\n$\n4. ALTERNATE # 3 PRICE\n$\n5. ALTERNATE # 4 PRICE\n$\n6. ALTERNATE # 5 PRICE\n$\n7. ALTERNATE # 6 PRICE\n$\n8. TOTAL BID PRICE\n$\nBID SECURITY: Bid Security Must Be in the Form of a Bid Bond Only and must be enclosed in the same envelope as the bid.\nBID BOND COMPANY:\n(BID BOND 10% OF BID)\nBIDDER:\n(FULL COMPANY NAME)\nPHONE/FAX/E-MAIL:\n\nN.Y.S. CERTIFIED MBE/WBE:\n(PLEASE PRINT WHICH ONE, IF NONE PLEASE PRINT N/A)\nEIN/SSN No.:\nBY:\n(PRINT NAME OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\n(SIGNATURE OF OWNER OR CORPORATE OFFICER)\nDATE:\nATTEST:\nNOTE:\n\n(EVERY SPACE MUST BE COMPLETED CORPORATE SEAL)\n(IF IT DOES NOT APPPLY, PLEASE INSERT N/A)\n\nIn case of any discrepancy between the price in words and that in figures the Lower Price Shall be considered the bid\nprice.\n*NAME OF THE PERSON OR FIRM THAT APPEARS ON THE LICENSE.\nALL BIDDERS: PLEASE USE THE FORM THAT IS PROVIEDED WITH THE PROJECT’S BID PACKAGE.\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\nBID FORM A-1\n\nEXHIBIT “A”\nARTICLE 15A\nMANDATORY NEW YORK STATE CERTIFIED\nMINORITY & WOMEN BUSINESS ENTERPRISES GOALS FOR SUBCONTRACTORS & SUPPLIES\n\nPROJECT NAME:\n\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump & Standpipe Replacement\n\nCONTRACT GOALS\nTOTAL % M/WBE GOAL\n30%\n\nContract # 1\n\nForm B‐1 “Bidder M/WBE Utilization Plan “in section “B” submitted by the lowest bidder will be compared to\nthe goals set forth above.\n\n14 A\n\nInsert bid breakdown pages\n\nOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nALTERNATES NO. 1 ‐ 6\n11202205: Bellevue Fire Pump &\nStandpipe Replacement\n\nNOTE:\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nThis solicitation contains Alternates 1‐6. The Corporation shall reserve the right select the Base Bid and /or\nAlternate No. 1 and / or Alternate No. 2. and/or Alternate No. 3., and/or Alternate No. , and/or Alternate No.\n5, and/or Alternate No. 6. In the event that the Corporation elects to award Alternate No. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 or any\ncombination of Alternates No. 1-6, the responsive bidder submitting the lowest aggregate bid price (Base Bid\n+ Alternates Selected at the NYC HHC's Discretion) shall be determined to be the apparent lowest bidder for\nthis solicitation. The responsive bidder submitting the lowest base bid shall be determined to be the apparent\nlow bidder for this solicitation.\n\nOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nATTACHMET NO. 1 TO BID PROPOSAL\nALL CONTRACTS\nNOTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 220 &\nNEW YORK LABOR LAW NO. 230\nAll contractors awarded contracts by New York City Health + Hospitals and all subcontractors working for those\ncontractors on New York City Health + Hospitals projects shall be required to notify each of their employees on\nsuch projects of the applicable prevailing wage for his or her job classification. This notification shall appear on\neach employee’s pay stub. In addition, the first paycheck given to employees at the project site, and the first\npaycheck given to employees at the project site after each successive July 1, shall be accompanied by a notice\nidentifying the public body. Such notice shall also inform employees of their right to contact the designated\npublic body if prevailing wages are not paid. Contact should be made through the Construction Management\nOffice of the New York City Health + Hospitals’ Facility where the work is being performed.\n\nAgreed:\nName of Contractor:\nBy: (Officer or Authorized) Representative: ________________________\nPrint\n__________________________________\nSignature\n\n__________________________\nDate\n\nTitle: ___________________________________________\nPrint\n\nBID FORM A‐1.1\n\nOffice of Facilities Development/ Contract Services\n55 Water Street, 25th Floor, New York, NY 10041\nTel: (212) 442‐3680 Fax: (212) 442‐3741\n\nName of Contractor: ___________________________\n\nProject Name: __________________________\n\nATTACHEMENT:\n\nNO. 2 TO BID PROPOSAL ‐ ALL CONTRACTS\n\nIMPROTANT:\n\nAll Insurance Carriers that will be providing coverage for New York Health + Hospitals\ncontacts shall be licensed and authorized/ admitted to be business in New York State.\n\nALL BIDDERS ARE REQUIRED TO COMPLETE THIS FORM AND SUBMIT IT WITH THEIR BID\n\nType of Coverage\n\nName of Insurance Carrier\n\nNAIC No.\n\nCommercial General Liability\nAutomobile Liability\nExcess/Umbrella\nWorker’s Compensation\nDisability Benefits\nAll Risk/Builders Risk\nIt is requested that an original Insurance Certificate substantiating the insurance coverage described above, be\nsubmitted to NYC H + H when the lowest responsive and responsible bidder returns its executed contract.\n\nSigned By: ________________________________________\n\nDate: ______________________________\n\nPrint Name: ________________________________________\nTitle: ______________________________________________\n\nBID FORM A‐1.2 Rev. 1/8/16\n\nFORM OF BID BOND\nKNOW ALL MEN BY THESE PRESENTS, that we__________________________________\n___________________________________________________________________________________\nhereinafter referred to as the “Principal,” and_______________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________\nHereinafter referred to as the “Surety” are held and firmly bound to the New York City Health and Hospitals\nCorporation hereinafter referred to as the “Corporation” or to its successors and assigns, in the penal sum\nof_________________________________________________________________________________\n($______________________) Dollars, lawful money of the United States for the payment of which said sum of money will\nand truly to be made, we, and each of us, bind ourselves, our heirs, executors, administrators, successors, and assigns,\njointly and severally, firmly by these presents.\nWHEREAS, the Principal is about to submit (or has submitted) to the Corporation the accompanying proposal,\nhereby made a part hereof, to enter into a contract in writing\nfor________________________________________________________________________________________________\n__________________________________________________________________________________________________\nNOW, THEREFORE, the conditions of this obligation are such that the Principal shall not withdraw any Proposals\nwithout the consent of the Corporation for a period of forty‐five (45) days after the opening of bids, one hundred\nand twenty (120) days after the opening of bids where the project has one or more contracts with a bid of one\nmillion dollars ($1,000,000) or more and, in event of acceptance of the Principal’s Proposals by the Corporation if\nthe Principal shall:\nA.\n\nwithin five (5) days after notification by the Corporation execute and deliver six (6) copies to the\nCorporation of all the executed counterparts of the Contract in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments, in accordance with proposal as accepted;\n\nB.\n\nfurnish a Performance Bond and separate Payment Bond, as may be required by the Corporation for the\nfaithful performance and proper fulfillment of such Contract, which bonds shall be satisfactory in all\nrespects to the Corporation, shall be executed by good and sufficient sureties; and;\n\nC.\n\nin all respects performs the agreement created by the acceptance of said Proposal as provided in the\ninformation for Bidders, bound herewith and hereby made a part hereof, or if the Corporation shall reject\nthe aforesaid Proposal, then this obligation shall be null and void; otherwise to remain in full force and\neffect.\n\nIn the event that the Proposal of the Principal shall be accepted and the Contract be awarded to him, the Surety\nhereunder agrees, subject only to the payment by the Principal of the premium therefore, if requested by the\nCorporation to write the aforementioned Performance and Payment bonds in the form set forth in the Contract\nDocuments.\nIt is expressly understood and agreed that the liability of the Surety for any and all claims hereunder shall in no\nevent exceed the penal amount of this obligation as herein stated.\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n‐16‐\n\nThere shall be no liability under this bond if, in the event of acceptance of the Principals Proposal by the Corporation,\neither a Performance Bond or Payment Bond or both, shall not be required by the Corporation on or before the 30th day\nafter the date on which the Corporation signs the Contract.\nThe Surety, for value received, hereby stipulates and agrees that the obligations of the Surety and its bond shall\nin no way be impaired or affected by any postponements of the day upon which the Corporation will receive or\nopen bids, or by any extensions of the time within which the Corporation may accept the Principal’s Proposal or\nby any waiver by the Corporation of the requirements of the Information for Bidders; and the Surety hereby\nwaives notice of any such postponements, extensions or waivers.\n\nSURETY COMPANY MUST BE LICENSED TO DO BUSINESS IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK\n\nINFORMATION FOR BIDDERS\n\nBID FORM A‐2\n\n‐17‐\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Principal and the Surety have hereunto set their hands and seeks and such of them\nas are a Corporation have caused their corporate seals to be hereto affixed and these presents to be signed by\ntheir proper officers the ______________________ day of _______________in the year__________.\nBY _________________________________ (L.S.)\n(Principal Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY__________________________________\n(Surety Signature)\n\n(Seal)\n\nBY _________________________________\n*****************\nACKNOWLEDGMENT OF PRINCIPAL, IF A CORPORATION\n\nSTATE OF :___________________________)\nSS:\nCOUNTY OF _________________________)\nOn this _____________________ day of ______________in the year____________ before me\npersonally came_____________________________ to me known, who being by me duly sworn\ndid depose and say that he resides at_________________________________________________\n_______________________________________________________________________________\nthat he is the __________________________ of________________________________________\n_______________________________________________________________________________\nthe corporation described in and which executed the foregoing instrument; that he knows the seal of said\ncorporation; that one of the seals affixed to said instrument is such seal; that it was affixed by one of the\ndirectors of said corporation, and that he signed his name there by like order.\n\n______________________________________\n(NOTARY SIGNATURE AND S