{"type":"message","id":"507c1757","parentId":"e3d20f58","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:24.104Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01X4ngWA2V99bTH8qaXpycwY","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SECTION 21 12 00\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes entire standpipe system from fire department connection to fire hose\nconnection and the following:\n1.\nComplete wet fire standpipe system.\n2.\nRoof manifold.\n3.\nAngle Hose Valves.\n4.\nFire Hose and Nozzles\n5.\nAccessories for Valves and Hoses.\n6.\nHose Valve Cabinets\n7.\nDetention Locked Hose Valve Cabinets\n8.\nPainting and Identification of piping.\n9.\nValve Supervisory Switches\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nDivision 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\nfor placement by this section.\n2.\nDivision 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\npainting specified by this section.\n3.\nSection 21 05 00 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product and\nexecution requirements for pipe, fittings, valves, hangers, supports, identification\nand painting for placement by this section.\n4.\nSection 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\nProduct requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n5.\nSection 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\nfor placement by this section.\n6.\nSection 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\nsprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 14 - Standard for the Installation of Standpipe, Private Hydrants and Hose\nSystems.\n\n1.03\nA.\n\nSUBMITTALS\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\nSubmittal procedures.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate supports, components, accessories and sizes.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog sheet for equipment indicating rough-in\nsize, finish, and accessories.\n\nD.\n\nField Test Reports: Indicate compliance with specified performance.\n\nE.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions: Submit with product data.\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.04\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit servicing requirements and test schedule.\n\n1.05\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nPerform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\nB.\n\nMaintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\n1.06\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n1.07\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\nRequirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\nB.\n\nDeliver and store products in shipping packaging until installation.\n\n1.08\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five-year manufacturer warranty for standpipes and valves.\n\n1.09\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish two (2) hose nozzles and hoses.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\nA.\n2.02\nA.\n\n2.03\n\nGENERAL\nAll threads are to conform to NYC Fire Department requirements.\nPIPE ESCUTCHEONS\nPipe escutcheons shall have an inside diameter closely fitting pipe outside diameter or\noutside of pipe insulation where pipe is insulated. Select outside diameter of\nescutcheon to completely cover pipe penetration hole in floors, walls, or ceilings; and\npipe sleeve extension, if any. Escutcheons shall be cast or sheet brass, solid or splithinged, with brass set screw. Provide chrome finish for occupied areas exposed to\nview.\nPIPE SLEEVES\n\nA.\n\nProvide pipe sleeves of one of the following. Pipe sleeve must be appropriate type and\nthickness for the UL firestopping assembly selected:\n1.\nSheet-Metal: Fabricate from galvanized sheet metal; round tube closed with\nsnaplock joint, welded spiral seams, or welded longitudinal joint. Fabricate from\nthe following gauges: 3\" and smaller, 20 gage minimum; 4\" to 6\", 16 gage; over\n6\", 14 gage minimum.\n2.\nSteel-Pipe: Fabricate from Schedule 40 galvanized steel pipe; remove burrs.\n3.\nIron-Pipe: Fabricate from cast-iron or ductile-iron pipe; remove burrs.\n4.\nFirestop penetration materials for sealing sleeves shall be listed by Underwriters\nLaboratories and if not listed have MEA or OTCR approval. The materials shall\nbe as specified in Section 07 27 0. For pipes passing through fire-rated floor,\ncast-in place firestop device with Underwriters Laboratories listing, and if not\nlisted have MEA or OTCR approval, is permitted as an acceptable sleeve\nalternative to a metallic sleeve with firestopping material. The cast-in place\ndevice is a one-step firestopping process that does not require additional firestop\npenetration materials for sealing the sleeves. The device shall be installed where\nrequired for sleeving purposes. The cast-in place firestop device shall not be used\nfor wall applications.\n\nB.\n\nMaterials for sealing space between each pipe and sleeve through non-rated interior\nwalls shall consist of mineral wool and sealant.\n\n2.04\n\nFIRE HOSE VALVES AND CABINETS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Roemer\n2.\nWSA Inc.\n3.\nCroker.\n\nB.\n\nCabinet: Suitable for 2-1/2” fire department valve and 1-1/2” hose rack assembly,\nrecessed, stainless steel 304 door with 20 gauge steel frame, dual horizontal panel, red\npowder coat finish, fire rated tub insulated with Firespan 90 tested by UL and rated to\nASTM E814. Similar to Croker 1410 Series Fire-Rated hose cabinet, rated to 2 hours.\n\nC.\n\nLocked Detention Cabinets: Constructed for maximum security facilities with 12 gauge\ncold rolled steel. Mitered and ground smooth corners. Cabinet shall be powder coated\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nwith thermally-fused polyester red finish. Heavy-duty continuous hinge. Door shall be\nflush solid metal with security-type lock. Recessed cabinet. Potter Roemer model#\nDC1810-F.\nD.\n\nHose Connection Valve: Angle type; brass finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 11/2 inch reducer, thread to match fire department hardware, with threaded cap and chain\nof brass finish. Hose valve shall conform to FDNY standards. Valves shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer Fig. 4065 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5015. Cap with chain shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer 4625 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5713. Threads shall be to NYC Fire\ndepartment specifications.\n\nE.\n\nHose Rack Assembly:\n1.\nSimilar to Croker Model 3307 Style N.\n2.\nUL 47, semiautomatic hose stations. Include brass rack nipple, hose rack, and\nthe following:\na.\nValve: UL 668, brass or bronze, 300-psig minimum pressure rating, 90degree-angle-pattern hose valve with female NPS inlet and outlet, brass\nfinish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-1/2 inch reducer, thread to\nmatch fire department hardware. Valve Operation: Nonadjustable type,\nunless pressure-regulating type is indicated. Hose Valve and Trim Finish:\nPolished chrome-plated.\nb.\nHose Rack: Steel; Semi-automatic swinging type with pins for folding\nhose and water stop. Finish: Red enamel.\nc.\nHose: NFPA 1961 and UL 219, lined fire hose, 1-1/2 inch diameter, 125\nfeet long, of polyurethane lined synthetic hose; mildew and rot-resistant.\nd.\nNozzle: UL 401, brass, combination fog, straight stream, and adjustable\nshut-off. Finish: polished brass.\ne.\nDrain Valves: UL 1726.\n\nF.\n\nPressure Restricting Hose Valve:\n1.\nPressure-Restricting Hose Valve Class: NPS 2-1/2” and 1-1/2”, brass, adjustable\nsimilar to Croker model 5560 set at 100 psi.\n\n2.05\nA.\n\nFIRE DEPARTMENT LOBBY HOSE CABINET\nFire Department Lobby Hose Cabinet:\n1.\nCabinet, with built-in storage shelf for storing below listed equipment, shall be\nrecessed type, 20-gage steel body and baked white polyester finish inside.\nExposed trim and door shall be 18-gage, with continuous steel hinge (brass pin).\nCabinet door shall have duo-panel wire inserted clear glass. Door shall be hinged\nright or left as required with lock and key in a key cabinet. Cabinet shall be\nPotter Roemer 1302 or Croker Corp. Fig. 2190. The cabinet shall be labeled “For\nFire Department Use Only”. Final size dependent on amount of material to be\nplaced in cabinet.\na.\nClass I standpipe requires the installation of a storage cabinet on the main\nentrance floor. Where one standpipe riser is installed in the building, the\ncabinet shall contain at least one fog nozzle, one 1½” spanner wrench, one\n2½” wrench, one 2½”x 1.5” non-swivel reducing coupling, and 125’ of\n1½” hose. Also provide one pressure restricting device to limit static and\nresidual pressures at the outlet of the hose connection to 100 psi. For\nbuildings over 10 stories, provide another cabinet at the tenth floor (and\nevery ten floors thereafter). Where two or more standpipe risers are\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nb.\nB.\n\n2.06\n\ninstalled in the building, at least two of the required items of equipment\nlisted herein shall be provided.\nThe equipment specified for the Lobby Storage Cabinet shall be of one\nmanufacturer for each complete unit.\n\nLobby Key Storage Cabinet:\n1.\nThe key to the “Lobby Storage Cabinet” shall be kept in a locked “Key Storage\nCabinet”, openable only by a Fire Department city wide standard key. The\ncabinet shall be labeled “For Fire Department Use Only”. A metal sign stating\nwhere the storage cabinet is located shall be placed in each stair enclosure on the\nmain entrance and on each floor. The cabinet shall hold a key for the lobby\nstorage cabinet. Cabinet installation requires 5”x5”x3” wall opening. Cabinet\nshall be Potter Roemer model #1950 NYFD Yale lock #SYA1, or Croker Fig.\n2928 or Fig. 2920.\nFIRE DEPARTMENT CONNECTION\n\nA.\n\nFlush type shall be of the size indicated on drawings. Fire Department connections shall\nbe polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves and cast iron plugs painted\nyellow with brass chain and with polished plate lettered “COMBINATION\nSTANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter inscription shall be either an\nintegral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate securely fastened to or above the\nFire Department connection. Flush type shall be Potter Roemer Fig. 5020G Series\n(THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig. 6030 Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads\nshall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nB.\n\nExposed type shall be of the size indicated on the drawings. Fire Department\nconnections shall be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves, pin lug\nswivels, plugs and chains painted yellow and with polished brass wall plate lettered\n“COMBINATION STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter\ninscription shall be either an integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate\nsecurely fastened to or above the Fire Department connection. Expose type shall be\nPotter- Roemer, Fig. 5750 Series (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig 6430\nSeries (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nC.\n\nOutlets: Two-way with fire department thread size. Threaded dust-cap and chain of\nmatching material and finish.\n\nD.\n\nDrain: 3/4 inch automatic drip pipe to outside or connected to drain via indirect drain.\n\nE.\n\nWhere a fence encloses a portion of the building containing a Fire Department\nconnection, Contractor shall provide and secure to the fence directly opposite the Fire\nDepartment connection a steel sign containing the following wording: \"F.D. Fire\nDepartment Connection located...Feet behind Sign.\" Sign shall be finished in porcelain\nenamel with 1-inch red letters on white background.\n\n2.07\n\nROOF MANIFOLD FIRE DEPARTMENT OUTLET CONNECTION:\n\nA.\n\nStyle: Free standing, angle inlet. Cast brass body.\n\nB.\n\nConnections: 6-inch female NPT inlet and four (4) 2-1/2-inch male NPT outlets.\n\nC.\n\nRoof outlet shall be fitted with three cast brass valves.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n2.08\n\nPRESSURE GAUGES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nTerice Model 600C\n2.\nWeksler Model Regal\n3.\nAGF Manufacturing Co.\n4.\nAMETEK, Inc.; U.S. Gauge.\n5.\nDresser Equipment Group; Instrument Div.\n\nB.\n\nDescription: UL 393, 4-1/2-inch- diameter, dial pressure gage with range of -10 to 300\npsig minimum. Cast brass, type ‘L’ case, glass covered, and phosphor bronze bourdon\ntype tube. Include caption \"WATER\" on dial face.\n\n2.09\nA.\n2.10\nA.\n\n2.11\n\nAUTOMATIC BALL DRIP\nAutomatic Ball Drip shall be 3/4\" Potter-Roemer Fig. 5982 or Croker Corp. Fig. 6781.\nLADDERS\nProvide permanent heavy steel ladders to provide access to valves in accordance with\nthe code requirements. Ladders shall be of width and height required, shall be made of\nheavy steel bars and heavy rungs and shall be permanently fastened at location. Where\nthe shut-off valve adjacent to the sprinkler alarm valve is located higher than 6' above\nthe floor, ladder shall be provided where directed.\nPAINTING\n\nA.\n\nPaints used on dedicated piping to combination sprinkler and standpipe shall not:\n1.\nExceed the VOC content limits established in the Green Seal Standard GS-11\nPaints, first edition, May 20, 1993.\n2.\nExceed the VOC content limit of 250 g/L established in the Green Seal Standard\nGC-03, Anti-Corrosive paints, second edition, January 7, 1997.\n\nB.\n\nProvide colors indicated in Paragraph 3.04\n1.\nFirst (1st) coat – Alkyd Vinyl Acrylic – Latex Primer – 1.2 Mills DFT\n2.\nSecond (2nd) coat – Semi-Gloss Vinyl Acrylic Latex – Enamel – 1.3 Mills DFT\n\n2.12\n\nVALVE SUPERVISORY SWITCHES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\n2.\nFire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\n3.\nKennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\n4.\nSystem Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n\nB.\n\nStandard: UL 346.\n\nC.\n\nType: Electrically supervised.\n\nD.\n\nComponents: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n\nE.\n\nDesign: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nF.\n\nLocate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted so not\nto interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to operate\nwithin two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved no more than\none-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch mechanism shall be\ncontained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing which shall provide 3/4” tapped\nconduit entrance and incorporate the necessary facilities for attachment to the valve.\nSwitch housings shall be finished in red baked enamel.\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n3.01\n\nEXAMINATION\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\nRequirements: Coordination and project conditions.\n\nB.\n\nVerify blocking in place for cabinet installation.\n\n3.02\n\nINSTALLATION\n\nA.\n\nInstall in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\nB.\n\nInstall cabinets plumb and level. Secure to adjacent surfaces. Establish top of cabinet\n(inside horizontal) surface 66 inches above finished floor.\n\nC.\n\nInstall hose station valve in cabinet at 60 inches above floor.\n\nD.\n\nConnect standpipe system to water source separate from domestic water connection.\n\nE.\n\nWhere static pressure exceeds 100 psi at any hose station, furnish pressure orifice disc\nin discharge of hose station valve to prevent pressure on hose exceeding 90 psi.\n\nF.\n\nInstall three-way fire department outlet on roof.\n\n3.03\n\nFIELD QUALITY CONTROL\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Quality Requirements,"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":640,"aggregated":"SECTION 21 12 00\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes entire standpipe system from fire department connection to fire hose\nconnection and the following:\n1.\nComplete wet fire standpipe system.\n2.\nRoof manifold.\n3.\nAngle Hose Valves.\n4.\nFire Hose and Nozzles\n5.\nAccessories for Valves and Hoses.\n6.\nHose Valve Cabinets\n7.\nDetention Locked Hose Valve Cabinets\n8.\nPainting and Identification of piping.\n9.\nValve Supervisory Switches\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nDivision 08 - Access Doors and Frames: Product requirements for access doors\nfor placement by this section.\n2.\nDivision 09 - Painting and Coating: Product and execution requirements for\npainting specified by this section.\n3.\nSection 21 05 00 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product and\nexecution requirements for pipe, fittings, valves, hangers, supports, identification\nand painting for placement by this section.\n4.\nSection 21 05 03 - Pipes Tubes for Fire-Suppression Piping and Equipment:\nProduct requirements for piping for placement by this section.\n5.\nSection 21 05 05 - Hangers and Supports for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pipe hangers and supports and firestopping\nfor placement by this section.\n6.\nSection 21 13 13 - Wet-Pipe Sprinkler Systems: Product requirements for wet\nsprinkler piping for placement by this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 14 - Standard for the Installation of Standpipe, Private Hydrants and Hose\nSystems.\n\n1.03\nA.\n\nSUBMITTALS\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal Procedures:\nSubmittal procedures.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate supports, components, accessories and sizes.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturer's catalog sheet for equipment indicating rough-in\nsize, finish, and accessories.\n\nD.\n\nField Test Reports: Indicate compliance with specified performance.\n\nE.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions: Submit with product data.\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\n1.04\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit servicing requirements and test schedule.\n\n1.05\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nPerform Work in accordance with NYCBC.\n\nB.\n\nMaintain one (1) copy of each document on site.\n\n1.06\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three (3) years documented experience.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\n1.07\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product Requirements:\nRequirements for transporting, handling, storing, and protecting products.\n\nB.\n\nDeliver and store products in shipping packaging until installation.\n\n1.08\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Product warranties and product bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five-year manufacturer warranty for standpipes and valves.\n\n1.09\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Execution and Closeout\nRequirements: Spare parts and maintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish two (2) hose nozzles and hoses.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\nA.\n2.02\nA.\n\n2.03\n\nGENERAL\nAll threads are to conform to NYC Fire Department requirements.\nPIPE ESCUTCHEONS\nPipe escutcheons shall have an inside diameter closely fitting pipe outside diameter or\noutside of pipe insulation where pipe is insulated. Select outside diameter of\nescutcheon to completely cover pipe penetration hole in floors, walls, or ceilings; and\npipe sleeve extension, if any. Escutcheons shall be cast or sheet brass, solid or splithinged, with brass set screw. Provide chrome finish for occupied areas exposed to\nview.\nPIPE SLEEVES\n\nA.\n\nProvide pipe sleeves of one of the following. Pipe sleeve must be appropriate type and\nthickness for the UL firestopping assembly selected:\n1.\nSheet-Metal: Fabricate from galvanized sheet metal; round tube closed with\nsnaplock joint, welded spiral seams, or welded longitudinal joint. Fabricate from\nthe following gauges: 3\" and smaller, 20 gage minimum; 4\" to 6\", 16 gage; over\n6\", 14 gage minimum.\n2.\nSteel-Pipe: Fabricate from Schedule 40 galvanized steel pipe; remove burrs.\n3.\nIron-Pipe: Fabricate from cast-iron or ductile-iron pipe; remove burrs.\n4.\nFirestop penetration materials for sealing sleeves shall be listed by Underwriters\nLaboratories and if not listed have MEA or OTCR approval. The materials shall\nbe as specified in Section 07 27 0. For pipes passing through fire-rated floor,\ncast-in place firestop device with Underwriters Laboratories listing, and if not\nlisted have MEA or OTCR approval, is permitted as an acceptable sleeve\nalternative to a metallic sleeve with firestopping material. The cast-in place\ndevice is a one-step firestopping process that does not require additional firestop\npenetration materials for sealing the sleeves. The device shall be installed where\nrequired for sleeving purposes. The cast-in place firestop device shall not be used\nfor wall applications.\n\nB.\n\nMaterials for sealing space between each pipe and sleeve through non-rated interior\nwalls shall consist of mineral wool and sealant.\n\n2.04\n\nFIRE HOSE VALVES AND CABINETS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Roemer\n2.\nWSA Inc.\n3.\nCroker.\n\nB.\n\nCabinet: Suitable for 2-1/2” fire department valve and 1-1/2” hose rack assembly,\nrecessed, stainless steel 304 door with 20 gauge steel frame, dual horizontal panel, red\npowder coat finish, fire rated tub insulated with Firespan 90 tested by UL and rated to\nASTM E814. Similar to Croker 1410 Series Fire-Rated hose cabinet, rated to 2 hours.\n\nC.\n\nLocked Detention Cabinets: Constructed for maximum security facilities with 12 gauge\ncold rolled steel. Mitered and ground smooth corners. Cabinet shall be powder coated\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nwith thermally-fused polyester red finish. Heavy-duty continuous hinge. Door shall be\nflush solid metal with security-type lock. Recessed cabinet. Potter Roemer model#\nDC1810-F.\nD.\n\nHose Connection Valve: Angle type; brass finish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 11/2 inch reducer, thread to match fire department hardware, with threaded cap and chain\nof brass finish. Hose valve shall conform to FDNY standards. Valves shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer Fig. 4065 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5015. Cap with chain shall be similar\nto Potter Roemer 4625 or Croker Corp. Fig. 5713. Threads shall be to NYC Fire\ndepartment specifications.\n\nE.\n\nHose Rack Assembly:\n1.\nSimilar to Croker Model 3307 Style N.\n2.\nUL 47, semiautomatic hose stations. Include brass rack nipple, hose rack, and\nthe following:\na.\nValve: UL 668, brass or bronze, 300-psig minimum pressure rating, 90degree-angle-pattern hose valve with female NPS inlet and outlet, brass\nfinish; 2-1/2 inch size with 2-1/2 inch by 1-1/2 inch reducer, thread to\nmatch fire department hardware. Valve Operation: Nonadjustable type,\nunless pressure-regulating type is indicated. Hose Valve and Trim Finish:\nPolished chrome-plated.\nb.\nHose Rack: Steel; Semi-automatic swinging type with pins for folding\nhose and water stop. Finish: Red enamel.\nc.\nHose: NFPA 1961 and UL 219, lined fire hose, 1-1/2 inch diameter, 125\nfeet long, of polyurethane lined synthetic hose; mildew and rot-resistant.\nd.\nNozzle: UL 401, brass, combination fog, straight stream, and adjustable\nshut-off. Finish: polished brass.\ne.\nDrain Valves: UL 1726.\n\nF.\n\nPressure Restricting Hose Valve:\n1.\nPressure-Restricting Hose Valve Class: NPS 2-1/2” and 1-1/2”, brass, adjustable\nsimilar to Croker model 5560 set at 100 psi.\n\n2.05\nA.\n\nFIRE DEPARTMENT LOBBY HOSE CABINET\nFire Department Lobby Hose Cabinet:\n1.\nCabinet, with built-in storage shelf for storing below listed equipment, shall be\nrecessed type, 20-gage steel body and baked white polyester finish inside.\nExposed trim and door shall be 18-gage, with continuous steel hinge (brass pin).\nCabinet door shall have duo-panel wire inserted clear glass. Door shall be hinged\nright or left as required with lock and key in a key cabinet. Cabinet shall be\nPotter Roemer 1302 or Croker Corp. Fig. 2190. The cabinet shall be labeled “For\nFire Department Use Only”. Final size dependent on amount of material to be\nplaced in cabinet.\na.\nClass I standpipe requires the installation of a storage cabinet on the main\nentrance floor. Where one standpipe riser is installed in the building, the\ncabinet shall contain at least one fog nozzle, one 1½” spanner wrench, one\n2½” wrench, one 2½”x 1.5” non-swivel reducing coupling, and 125’ of\n1½” hose. Also provide one pressure restricting device to limit static and\nresidual pressures at the outlet of the hose connection to 100 psi. For\nbuildings over 10 stories, provide another cabinet at the tenth floor (and\nevery ten floors thereafter). Where two or more standpipe risers are\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nb.\nB.\n\n2.06\n\ninstalled in the building, at least two of the required items of equipment\nlisted herein shall be provided.\nThe equipment specified for the Lobby Storage Cabinet shall be of one\nmanufacturer for each complete unit.\n\nLobby Key Storage Cabinet:\n1.\nThe key to the “Lobby Storage Cabinet” shall be kept in a locked “Key Storage\nCabinet”, openable only by a Fire Department city wide standard key. The\ncabinet shall be labeled “For Fire Department Use Only”. A metal sign stating\nwhere the storage cabinet is located shall be placed in each stair enclosure on the\nmain entrance and on each floor. The cabinet shall hold a key for the lobby\nstorage cabinet. Cabinet installation requires 5”x5”x3” wall opening. Cabinet\nshall be Potter Roemer model #1950 NYFD Yale lock #SYA1, or Croker Fig.\n2928 or Fig. 2920.\nFIRE DEPARTMENT CONNECTION\n\nA.\n\nFlush type shall be of the size indicated on drawings. Fire Department connections shall\nbe polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves and cast iron plugs painted\nyellow with brass chain and with polished plate lettered “COMBINATION\nSTANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter inscription shall be either an\nintegral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate securely fastened to or above the\nFire Department connection. Flush type shall be Potter Roemer Fig. 5020G Series\n(THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig. 6030 Series (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads\nshall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nB.\n\nExposed type shall be of the size indicated on the drawings. Fire Department\nconnections shall be polished brass with two individual drop clapper valves, pin lug\nswivels, plugs and chains painted yellow and with polished brass wall plate lettered\n“COMBINATION STANDPIPE AND SPRINKLER SYSTEMS”. The letter\ninscription shall be either an integral part of the plate or on a separate nameplate\nsecurely fastened to or above the Fire Department connection. Expose type shall be\nPotter- Roemer, Fig. 5750 Series (THREADS: N.Y.F.D.) or Croker Corp. Fig 6430\nSeries (3” NYCFD inlets). Threads shall be to NYC Fire Department specifications.\n\nC.\n\nOutlets: Two-way with fire department thread size. Threaded dust-cap and chain of\nmatching material and finish.\n\nD.\n\nDrain: 3/4 inch automatic drip pipe to outside or connected to drain via indirect drain.\n\nE.\n\nWhere a fence encloses a portion of the building containing a Fire Department\nconnection, Contractor shall provide and secure to the fence directly opposite the Fire\nDepartment connection a steel sign containing the following wording: \"F.D. Fire\nDepartment Connection located...Feet behind Sign.\" Sign shall be finished in porcelain\nenamel with 1-inch red letters on white background.\n\n2.07\n\nROOF MANIFOLD FIRE DEPARTMENT OUTLET CONNECTION:\n\nA.\n\nStyle: Free standing, angle inlet. Cast brass body.\n\nB.\n\nConnections: 6-inch female NPT inlet and four (4) 2-1/2-inch male NPT outlets.\n\nC.\n\nRoof outlet shall be fitted with three cast brass valves.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n2.08\n\nPRESSURE GAUGES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nTerice Model 600C\n2.\nWeksler Model Regal\n3.\nAGF Manufacturing Co.\n4.\nAMETEK, Inc.; U.S. Gauge.\n5.\nDresser Equipment Group; Instrument Div.\n\nB.\n\nDescription: UL 393, 4-1/2-inch- diameter, dial pressure gage with range of -10 to 300\npsig minimum. Cast brass, type ‘L’ case, glass covered, and phosphor bronze bourdon\ntype tube. Include caption \"WATER\" on dial face.\n\n2.09\nA.\n2.10\nA.\n\n2.11\n\nAUTOMATIC BALL DRIP\nAutomatic Ball Drip shall be 3/4\" Potter-Roemer Fig. 5982 or Croker Corp. Fig. 6781.\nLADDERS\nProvide permanent heavy steel ladders to provide access to valves in accordance with\nthe code requirements. Ladders shall be of width and height required, shall be made of\nheavy steel bars and heavy rungs and shall be permanently fastened at location. Where\nthe shut-off valve adjacent to the sprinkler alarm valve is located higher than 6' above\nthe floor, ladder shall be provided where directed.\nPAINTING\n\nA.\n\nPaints used on dedicated piping to combination sprinkler and standpipe shall not:\n1.\nExceed the VOC content limits established in the Green Seal Standard GS-11\nPaints, first edition, May 20, 1993.\n2.\nExceed the VOC content limit of 250 g/L established in the Green Seal Standard\nGC-03, Anti-Corrosive paints, second edition, January 7, 1997.\n\nB.\n\nProvide colors indicated in Paragraph 3.04\n1.\nFirst (1st) coat – Alkyd Vinyl Acrylic – Latex Primer – 1.2 Mills DFT\n2.\nSecond (2nd) coat – Semi-Gloss Vinyl Acrylic Latex – Enamel – 1.3 Mills DFT\n\n2.12\n\nVALVE SUPERVISORY SWITCHES\n\nA.\n\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPotter Electric Signal Co. Model OSYSU-2\n2.\nFire-Lite Alarms, Inc.; a Honeywell company.\n3.\nKennedy Valve; a division of McWane, Inc.\n4.\nSystem Sensor; a Honeywell company.\n\nB.\n\nStandard: UL 346.\n\nC.\n\nType: Electrically supervised.\n\nD.\n\nComponents: Single-pole, double-throw switch with normally closed contacts.\n\nE.\n\nDesign: Signals that controlled valve is in other than fully open position.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE-SUPPRESSION STANDPIPES\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 12 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nF.\n\nLocate on each valve as designated on the drawings. Switches shall be mounted so not\nto interfere with the normal operation of the valve and shall be adjusted to operate\nwithin two revolutions of the valve control or when the stem has moved no more than\none-fifth of the distance from its normal position. The switch mechanism shall be\ncontained in a weatherproof die-cast aluminum housing which shall provide 3/4” tapped\nconduit entrance and incorporate the necessary facilities for attachment to the valve.\nSwitch housings shall be finished in red baked enamel.\n\nPART 3 - EXECUTION\n3.01\n\nEXAMINATION\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Administrative\nRequirements: Coordination and project conditions.\n\nB.\n\nVerify blocking in place for cabinet installation.\n\n3.02\n\nINSTALLATION\n\nA.\n\nInstall in accordance with NFPA 14.\n\nB.\n\nInstall cabinets plumb and level. Secure to adjacent surfaces. Establish top of cabinet\n(inside horizontal) surface 66 inches above finished floor.\n\nC.\n\nInstall hose station valve in cabinet at 60 inches above floor.\n\nD.\n\nConnect standpipe system to water source separate from domestic water connection.\n\nE.\n\nWhere static pressure exceeds 100 psi at any hose station, furnish pressure orifice disc\nin discharge of hose station valve to prevent pressure on hose exceeding 90 psi.\n\nF.\n\nInstall three-way fire department outlet on roof.\n\n3.03\n\nFIELD QUALITY CONTROL\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Quality Requirements,","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138624096}}
{"type":"message","id":"937a8872","parentId":"507c1757","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:24.780Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_012asKtTv7vb6PwmuTjFjdot","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SECTION 21 30 00\nFIRE PUMPS\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes\n1.\nFire pump package and motor.\n2.\nControllers for electric fire pumps.\n3.\nElectric jockey pump.\n4.\nControllers for pressure-maintenance pumps.\n5.\nFire-pump accessories and specialties\n6.\nFlowmeter Systems\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nSection 210500 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product\nrequirements for Fire piping placement by this section.\n2.\nSection 21 05 48 - Noise and Vibration Controls for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pump isolators for placement by this\nsection.\n3.\nDivision 26 - Wiring Connections: Execution requirements for pumps specified\nby this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Electrical Manufacturers Association:\n1.\nNEMA 250 - Enclosures for Electrical Equipment (1000 Volts Maximum).\n2.\nNEMA MG 1 - Motors and Generators.\n\nC.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 13 - Installation of Sprinkler Systems.\n2.\nNFPA 14 – Installation of Standpipe and Hose Systems.\n3.\nNFPA 20 - Standard for the Installation of Centrifugal Fire Pumps.\n\nD.\n\nUnderwriters Laboratories Inc.:\n1.\nUL 448 - Pumps for Fire Protection Service.\n2.\nUL 778 - Motor Operated Water Pumps.\n3.\nUL 1478 - Fire Pump Relief Valves.\n4.\nUL - Fire Protection Equipment Directory.\n\n1.03\n\nDESIGN REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nFire Pump System: The fire pump system consists of an (horizontal split-case) fire\npump motor, automatic transfer switch, soft starting fire pump controller, jockey pump,\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\njockey pump motor, jockey pump controller, associated valves, gauges, and test\napparatus to supply water to the combined standpipe & sprinkler system.\n1.\nThe jockey pump maintains a minimum pressure in the combined standpipe &\nsprinkler system.\n2.\nThe fire pump starts in the event of a drop in pressure below the minimum\npressure maintained by the jockey pump.\nC.\n\n1.04\n\nDesign Parameters\n1.\nSize of selected pump is not to be changed from that shown on the Contract\nDrawings unless shown to be inadequate as per calculations to be provided in the\nsprinkler/standpipe system.\n2.\nSubmittals in this section shall not be made until hydraulic calculations provided\nhave been submitted and reviewed.\n3.\nFire pump and controller shall be delivered “broken down” for transport into the\nfire pump room, and field assembled.\nPERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nSeismic Performance: Fire pumps shall withstand the effects of earthquake motions\ndetermined according to ASCE/SEI 7.\n1.\nThe term \"withstand\" means \"the unit will remain in place without separation of\nany parts from the device when subjected to the seismic forces specified and the\nunit will be fully operational after the seismic event.\"\n\nC.\n\nPump Equipment, Accessory, and Specialty Pressure Rating: 300 psig minimum unless\nhigher pressure rating is indicated.\n\n1.05\n\nSUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal procedures.\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate layout, general assembly, components, dimensions, weights,\nclearances and methods of assembly.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturers literature including general assembly, pump curves\nshowing performance characteristics with pump and system, operating point indicated,\nNPSH curve, controls, wiring diagrams and service connections. All Shop Drawings\nshall also be submitted to Electrical for approval.\n\nD.\n\nRigging: The contractor shall submit a rigging plan for bringing the fire pump and\ncontroller/transfer switch to the fire pump room prior to commencing with such work.\n\nE.\n\nTest Reports:\n1.\nFactory performance test: certified test curve for each pump.\n2.\nField acceptance test: Indicate results of hydrostatic test and field acceptance\ntests.\n3.\nComply with Modified NYC Fire Code Chapter 9 Section BC 901 (901.5)\n(Acceptance Test).\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions:\nrequirements, for fire pump system.\n\nSubmit\n\nsupport\n\ndetails,\n\nconnection\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nG.\n\nSeismic Qualification Certificates: For fire pumps, accessories, and components, from\nmanufacturer.\n1.\nBasis for Certification: Indicate whether withstand certification is based on\nactual test of assembled components or on calculation.\n2.\nDimensioned Outline Drawings of Equipment Unit: Identify center of gravity\nand locate and describe mounting and anchorage provisions.\n3.\nDetailed description of equipment anchorage devices on which the certification is\nbased and their installation requirements.\n\nH.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\nI.\n\nContractor’s written narrative identifying the specific method of performing the fire\npump flow test, including safety measures for personnel and means for draining the\nwater from the roof so as not to overload the roof or damage the building.\n\n1.06\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nProject Record Documents: Record actual locations of components and accessories.\n\nC.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit manufacturer’s literature, cleaning\nprocedures, replacement parts lists, and repair data for pumps, drivers and controllers.\n\n1.07\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nElectrical Components, Devices, and Accessories: Listed and labeled as defined in\nNFPA 70, by a qualified testing agency, and marked for intended location and\napplication.\n\nB.\n\nNFPA Compliance: Comply with NFPA 20, \"Installation of Stationary Pumps for Fire\nProtection.\"\n\nC.\n\nMaintain one copy of each document on site.\n\n1.08\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three years documented experience, and with service facilities\nwithin 100 miles of Project.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\nC.\n\nDesign fire pump system under direct supervision of Professional Engineer experienced\nin design of this Work and licensed in the State of New York.\n\n1.09\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product storage and\nhandling requirements.\n\nB.\n\nAccept fire pumps and components on site in factory packing. Inspect for damage.\nComply with manufacturers rigging and installation instructions.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nC.\n\nProtect fire pumps and components from physical damage including effects of weather,\nwater, and construction debris.\n\nD.\n\nFurnish temporary, inlet and outlet caps and maintain in place until installation.\n\n1.10\n\nCOORDINATION\n\nA.\n\nCoordinate layout and installation of controllers with other construction including\nconduit, piping, fire-pump equipment, and adjacent surfaces. Maintain required\nclearances for workspace and equipment access doors and panels. Ensure that\ncontrollers are within sight of fire-pump drivers.\n\nB.\n\nCoordinate sizes and locations of concrete bases with actual equipment provided.\n\n1.11\n\nFIELD MEASUREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nVerify field measurements prior to fabrication.\n\nB.\n\nCoordinate sizes and locations of concrete bases with actual equipment provided.\n\n1.12\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product warranties and\nproduct bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five -year manufacturer warranty for fire pumps.\n\n1.13\n\nMAINTENANCE SERVICE\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Maintenance service.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish service and maintenance of fire pump, driver, and controller for five (5) years\nfrom Date of Substantial Completion.\n\n1.14\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Spare parts and\nmaintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish one (1) set of gaskets, screens and seals for each pump type and model\nsupplied.\n\nC.\n\nFurnish for each controller packaged with protective covering for storage and identified\nwith labels describing contents:\n1.\nIndicating Lights: Two (2) of each type and color of lens installed; two (2) of\neach type and size of lamp installed.\n2.\nAuxiliary Contacts: One (1) for each size and type of magnetic contactor\ninstalled.\n3.\nPower Contacts: Three (3) for each size and type of magnetic contactor installed.\n4.\nContactor Coils: One (1) for each size and type of magnetic controller installed.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\n\nGENERAL\n\nA.\n\nDescription: Factory-tested fire-pump and driver unit.\n\nB.\n\nBase: Fabricated and attached to fire-pump and driver unit with reinforcement to resist\nmovement of pump during seismic events when base is anchored to building substrate.\n\nC.\n\nFinish: Red paint applied to factory-assembled and -tested unit before shipping.\n\nD.\n\nClearances at the access to the cellar fire pump room are limited. Coordinate with\navailable space at stair turns. Deliver the fire pump and controller “broken down” for\ntransportation to the designated fire pump room.\n\n2.02\nA.\n\n2.03\n\nFIRE PUMPS\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPeerless Pump\n2.\nPatterson\n3.\nAurora\nVERTICAL IN-LINE PUMPS\n\nA.\n\nType: UL 448, vertical, single stage, close coupled, radial split casing, for in-line\nmounting.\n\nB.\n\nCasting: Cast or ductile iron, with suction and discharge gage port, casing wear ring,\nseal flush connection, drain plug, flanged suction and discharge.\n\nC.\n\nImpeller: Bronze, fully enclosed, keyed directly to motor shaft.\n\nD.\n\nShaft: Solid alloy steel with bronze sleeve.\n\n2.04\n\nCENTRIFUGAL FIRE PUMPS\n\nA.\n\nDescription, General: New York City MEA or BS&A approved, UL 448 Listed and\nFM Approved factory-assembled and -tested, electric-drive, centrifugal fire pumps\ncapable of furnishing not less than 150 percent of rated capacity at not less than 65\npercent of total rated head and with shutoff head limited to 140 percent of total rated\nhead.\n1.\nFinish: Manufacturer's standard red paint applied to factory-assembled and tested unit before shipping.\n2.\nNameplate: Complete with capacities, characteristics, and other pertinent data.\n\nB.\n\nFabricate bases for fire pumps, pressure-maintenance pumps, and controllers (unless\nwall mounted) with reinforcement to resist movement of pumps and controllers during a\nseismic event when their bases are anchored to building structure.\n\nC.\n\nHorizontally Mounted, Split-Case Fire Pumps with pump and driver mounted on same\nbase and connected with coupling.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nD.\n\nCoupling:\nFlexible and capable of absorbing torsional vibration and shaft\nmisalignment. Include metal coupling guard. Do not use elastomeric (plastic)\ncouplings\n\nE.\n\nCasing: Cast or ductile iron, with suction and discharge gage port, casing wear ring,\nseal flush connection, drain plug, flanged suction and discharge.\n\nF.\n\nImpeller: Bronze construction, statically and dynamically balanced, and keyed to shaft.\n\nG.\n\nShaft: Solid alloy steel with bronze sleeve.\n1.\nShaft Bearings: Grease-lubricated ball bearings in cast-iron housing.\n2.\nSeals: Stuffing box with minimum of four rings of graphite-impregnated braided\nyarn and bronze packing gland.\n\nH.\n\nSeal: Packing gland with minimum four rings graphite impregnated packing and bronze\nlantern rings, 230 degrees F maximum continuous operating temperature.\n\nI.\n\nDriver: UL-listed, NEMA MG 1, open-dripproof, squirrel-cage, induction motor\ncomplying with NFPA 20 and NFPA 70. Include wiring compatible with controller\nused.\n1.\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by\none of the following:\na.\nPeerless\nb.\nAurora\nc.\nPatterson\n\nJ.\n\nFire-Pump Performance Characteristics: Refer to schedules on Drawings for additional\nmodel information.\n1.\nRated Capacity: as listed on Design Drawings\n2.\nInlet Flange: 300 lbs, ductile iron flange.\n3.\nOutlet Flange: 300 lbs, ductile iron flange.\n4.\nMotor Horsepower: as listed on Design Drawings\n\n2.05\n\nFIRE PUMP CONTROLLER\n\nA.\n\nPump Controllers, General: UL 218 and NFPA 20; UL listed and FM approved for\nfire/sprinkler booster pump service, suitable for use with the electric motor to be used;\ncombined automatic and manual operation; factory tested for capacities and electrical\ncharacteristics required. Mark controller “Fire Pump Controller”.\n\nB.\n\nMounting: Floor-stand type for field electrical connections on the pump base.\n\nC.\n\nStandards, Listings & Approvals:\n1.\nThe controller shall conform to all the requirements of the latest editions of:\nNFPA 70, National Electric Code.\n2.\nThe controller shall be listed by: Underwriters Laboratories, Inc., in accordance\nwith UL508A, Standard for Industrial Controls.\n3.\nThe controller shall be approved by: Factory Mutual (IEC 62091).\n\nD.\n\nController: UL listed, soft start fire pump controller with automatic transfer switch, in\nNEMA 250 Types 2 and 12 enclosure, including the following:\n1.\nDisconnect Switch: Externally operable, quick break type.\n2.\nCircuit Breaker: Size to NFPA 20, minimum 100,000 amperes interrupting\ncapacity.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n3.\n4.\n5."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":674,"aggregated":"SECTION 21 30 00\nFIRE PUMPS\nPART 1 - GENERAL\n1.01\n\nSUMMARY\n\nA.\n\nSection includes\n1.\nFire pump package and motor.\n2.\nControllers for electric fire pumps.\n3.\nElectric jockey pump.\n4.\nControllers for pressure-maintenance pumps.\n5.\nFire-pump accessories and specialties\n6.\nFlowmeter Systems\n\nB.\n\nRelated Sections:\n1.\nSection 210500 - Common Work Results for Fire Suppression: Product\nrequirements for Fire piping placement by this section.\n2.\nSection 21 05 48 - Noise and Vibration Controls for Fire-Suppression Piping and\nEquipment: Product requirements for pump isolators for placement by this\nsection.\n3.\nDivision 26 - Wiring Connections: Execution requirements for pumps specified\nby this section.\n\n1.02\n\nREFERENCES\n\nA.\n\nFM Global:\n1.\nFM - Approval Guide, A Guide to Equipment, Materials & Services Approved\nBy Factory Mutual Research For Property Conservation.\n\nB.\n\nNational Electrical Manufacturers Association:\n1.\nNEMA 250 - Enclosures for Electrical Equipment (1000 Volts Maximum).\n2.\nNEMA MG 1 - Motors and Generators.\n\nC.\n\nNational Fire Protection Association:\n1.\nNFPA 13 - Installation of Sprinkler Systems.\n2.\nNFPA 14 – Installation of Standpipe and Hose Systems.\n3.\nNFPA 20 - Standard for the Installation of Centrifugal Fire Pumps.\n\nD.\n\nUnderwriters Laboratories Inc.:\n1.\nUL 448 - Pumps for Fire Protection Service.\n2.\nUL 778 - Motor Operated Water Pumps.\n3.\nUL 1478 - Fire Pump Relief Valves.\n4.\nUL - Fire Protection Equipment Directory.\n\n1.03\n\nDESIGN REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nFire Pump System: The fire pump system consists of an (horizontal split-case) fire\npump motor, automatic transfer switch, soft starting fire pump controller, jockey pump,\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 1\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\njockey pump motor, jockey pump controller, associated valves, gauges, and test\napparatus to supply water to the combined standpipe & sprinkler system.\n1.\nThe jockey pump maintains a minimum pressure in the combined standpipe &\nsprinkler system.\n2.\nThe fire pump starts in the event of a drop in pressure below the minimum\npressure maintained by the jockey pump.\nC.\n\n1.04\n\nDesign Parameters\n1.\nSize of selected pump is not to be changed from that shown on the Contract\nDrawings unless shown to be inadequate as per calculations to be provided in the\nsprinkler/standpipe system.\n2.\nSubmittals in this section shall not be made until hydraulic calculations provided\nhave been submitted and reviewed.\n3.\nFire pump and controller shall be delivered “broken down” for transport into the\nfire pump room, and field assembled.\nPERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nConform to NFPA 20.\n\nB.\n\nSeismic Performance: Fire pumps shall withstand the effects of earthquake motions\ndetermined according to ASCE/SEI 7.\n1.\nThe term \"withstand\" means \"the unit will remain in place without separation of\nany parts from the device when subjected to the seismic forces specified and the\nunit will be fully operational after the seismic event.\"\n\nC.\n\nPump Equipment, Accessory, and Specialty Pressure Rating: 300 psig minimum unless\nhigher pressure rating is indicated.\n\n1.05\n\nSUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Submittal procedures.\n\nB.\n\nShop Drawings: Indicate layout, general assembly, components, dimensions, weights,\nclearances and methods of assembly.\n\nC.\n\nProduct Data: Submit manufacturers literature including general assembly, pump curves\nshowing performance characteristics with pump and system, operating point indicated,\nNPSH curve, controls, wiring diagrams and service connections. All Shop Drawings\nshall also be submitted to Electrical for approval.\n\nD.\n\nRigging: The contractor shall submit a rigging plan for bringing the fire pump and\ncontroller/transfer switch to the fire pump room prior to commencing with such work.\n\nE.\n\nTest Reports:\n1.\nFactory performance test: certified test curve for each pump.\n2.\nField acceptance test: Indicate results of hydrostatic test and field acceptance\ntests.\n3.\nComply with Modified NYC Fire Code Chapter 9 Section BC 901 (901.5)\n(Acceptance Test).\n\nF.\n\nManufacturer's Installation Instructions:\nrequirements, for fire pump system.\n\nSubmit\n\nsupport\n\ndetails,\n\nconnection\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 2\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nG.\n\nSeismic Qualification Certificates: For fire pumps, accessories, and components, from\nmanufacturer.\n1.\nBasis for Certification: Indicate whether withstand certification is based on\nactual test of assembled components or on calculation.\n2.\nDimensioned Outline Drawings of Equipment Unit: Identify center of gravity\nand locate and describe mounting and anchorage provisions.\n3.\nDetailed description of equipment anchorage devices on which the certification is\nbased and their installation requirements.\n\nH.\n\nManufacturer's Certificate: Certify products meet or exceed specified requirements.\n\nI.\n\nContractor’s written narrative identifying the specific method of performing the fire\npump flow test, including safety measures for personnel and means for draining the\nwater from the roof so as not to overload the roof or damage the building.\n\n1.06\n\nCLOSEOUT SUBMITTALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Closeout procedures.\n\nB.\n\nProject Record Documents: Record actual locations of components and accessories.\n\nC.\n\nOperation and Maintenance Data: Submit manufacturer’s literature, cleaning\nprocedures, replacement parts lists, and repair data for pumps, drivers and controllers.\n\n1.07\n\nQUALITY ASSURANCE\n\nA.\n\nElectrical Components, Devices, and Accessories: Listed and labeled as defined in\nNFPA 70, by a qualified testing agency, and marked for intended location and\napplication.\n\nB.\n\nNFPA Compliance: Comply with NFPA 20, \"Installation of Stationary Pumps for Fire\nProtection.\"\n\nC.\n\nMaintain one copy of each document on site.\n\n1.08\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nA.\n\nManufacturer: Company specializing in manufacturing products specified in this\nsection with minimum three years documented experience, and with service facilities\nwithin 100 miles of Project.\n\nB.\n\nInstaller: Company specializing in performing Work of this section with minimum three\n(3) years documented experience approved by manufacturer.\n\nC.\n\nDesign fire pump system under direct supervision of Professional Engineer experienced\nin design of this Work and licensed in the State of New York.\n\n1.09\n\nDELIVERY, STORAGE AND HANDLING\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product storage and\nhandling requirements.\n\nB.\n\nAccept fire pumps and components on site in factory packing. Inspect for damage.\nComply with manufacturers rigging and installation instructions.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 3\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nC.\n\nProtect fire pumps and components from physical damage including effects of weather,\nwater, and construction debris.\n\nD.\n\nFurnish temporary, inlet and outlet caps and maintain in place until installation.\n\n1.10\n\nCOORDINATION\n\nA.\n\nCoordinate layout and installation of controllers with other construction including\nconduit, piping, fire-pump equipment, and adjacent surfaces. Maintain required\nclearances for workspace and equipment access doors and panels. Ensure that\ncontrollers are within sight of fire-pump drivers.\n\nB.\n\nCoordinate sizes and locations of concrete bases with actual equipment provided.\n\n1.11\n\nFIELD MEASUREMENTS\n\nA.\n\nVerify field measurements prior to fabrication.\n\nB.\n\nCoordinate sizes and locations of concrete bases with actual equipment provided.\n\n1.12\n\nWARRANTY\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Product warranties and\nproduct bonds.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish five -year manufacturer warranty for fire pumps.\n\n1.13\n\nMAINTENANCE SERVICE\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Maintenance service.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish service and maintenance of fire pump, driver, and controller for five (5) years\nfrom Date of Substantial Completion.\n\n1.14\n\nEXTRA MATERIALS\n\nA.\n\nInformation for Bidders, Bid Agreement General Conditions - Spare parts and\nmaintenance products.\n\nB.\n\nFurnish one (1) set of gaskets, screens and seals for each pump type and model\nsupplied.\n\nC.\n\nFurnish for each controller packaged with protective covering for storage and identified\nwith labels describing contents:\n1.\nIndicating Lights: Two (2) of each type and color of lens installed; two (2) of\neach type and size of lamp installed.\n2.\nAuxiliary Contacts: One (1) for each size and type of magnetic contactor\ninstalled.\n3.\nPower Contacts: Three (3) for each size and type of magnetic contactor installed.\n4.\nContactor Coils: One (1) for each size and type of magnetic controller installed.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 4\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nPART 2 - PRODUCTS\n2.01\n\nGENERAL\n\nA.\n\nDescription: Factory-tested fire-pump and driver unit.\n\nB.\n\nBase: Fabricated and attached to fire-pump and driver unit with reinforcement to resist\nmovement of pump during seismic events when base is anchored to building substrate.\n\nC.\n\nFinish: Red paint applied to factory-assembled and -tested unit before shipping.\n\nD.\n\nClearances at the access to the cellar fire pump room are limited. Coordinate with\navailable space at stair turns. Deliver the fire pump and controller “broken down” for\ntransportation to the designated fire pump room.\n\n2.02\nA.\n\n2.03\n\nFIRE PUMPS\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by one of\nthe following:\n1.\nPeerless Pump\n2.\nPatterson\n3.\nAurora\nVERTICAL IN-LINE PUMPS\n\nA.\n\nType: UL 448, vertical, single stage, close coupled, radial split casing, for in-line\nmounting.\n\nB.\n\nCasting: Cast or ductile iron, with suction and discharge gage port, casing wear ring,\nseal flush connection, drain plug, flanged suction and discharge.\n\nC.\n\nImpeller: Bronze, fully enclosed, keyed directly to motor shaft.\n\nD.\n\nShaft: Solid alloy steel with bronze sleeve.\n\n2.04\n\nCENTRIFUGAL FIRE PUMPS\n\nA.\n\nDescription, General: New York City MEA or BS&A approved, UL 448 Listed and\nFM Approved factory-assembled and -tested, electric-drive, centrifugal fire pumps\ncapable of furnishing not less than 150 percent of rated capacity at not less than 65\npercent of total rated head and with shutoff head limited to 140 percent of total rated\nhead.\n1.\nFinish: Manufacturer's standard red paint applied to factory-assembled and tested unit before shipping.\n2.\nNameplate: Complete with capacities, characteristics, and other pertinent data.\n\nB.\n\nFabricate bases for fire pumps, pressure-maintenance pumps, and controllers (unless\nwall mounted) with reinforcement to resist movement of pumps and controllers during a\nseismic event when their bases are anchored to building structure.\n\nC.\n\nHorizontally Mounted, Split-Case Fire Pumps with pump and driver mounted on same\nbase and connected with coupling.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 5\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\nD.\n\nCoupling:\nFlexible and capable of absorbing torsional vibration and shaft\nmisalignment. Include metal coupling guard. Do not use elastomeric (plastic)\ncouplings\n\nE.\n\nCasing: Cast or ductile iron, with suction and discharge gage port, casing wear ring,\nseal flush connection, drain plug, flanged suction and discharge.\n\nF.\n\nImpeller: Bronze construction, statically and dynamically balanced, and keyed to shaft.\n\nG.\n\nShaft: Solid alloy steel with bronze sleeve.\n1.\nShaft Bearings: Grease-lubricated ball bearings in cast-iron housing.\n2.\nSeals: Stuffing box with minimum of four rings of graphite-impregnated braided\nyarn and bronze packing gland.\n\nH.\n\nSeal: Packing gland with minimum four rings graphite impregnated packing and bronze\nlantern rings, 230 degrees F maximum continuous operating temperature.\n\nI.\n\nDriver: UL-listed, NEMA MG 1, open-dripproof, squirrel-cage, induction motor\ncomplying with NFPA 20 and NFPA 70. Include wiring compatible with controller\nused.\n1.\nManufacturers: Subject to compliance with requirements, provide products by\none of the following:\na.\nPeerless\nb.\nAurora\nc.\nPatterson\n\nJ.\n\nFire-Pump Performance Characteristics: Refer to schedules on Drawings for additional\nmodel information.\n1.\nRated Capacity: as listed on Design Drawings\n2.\nInlet Flange: 300 lbs, ductile iron flange.\n3.\nOutlet Flange: 300 lbs, ductile iron flange.\n4.\nMotor Horsepower: as listed on Design Drawings\n\n2.05\n\nFIRE PUMP CONTROLLER\n\nA.\n\nPump Controllers, General: UL 218 and NFPA 20; UL listed and FM approved for\nfire/sprinkler booster pump service, suitable for use with the electric motor to be used;\ncombined automatic and manual operation; factory tested for capacities and electrical\ncharacteristics required. Mark controller “Fire Pump Controller”.\n\nB.\n\nMounting: Floor-stand type for field electrical connections on the pump base.\n\nC.\n\nStandards, Listings & Approvals:\n1.\nThe controller shall conform to all the requirements of the latest editions of:\nNFPA 70, National Electric Code.\n2.\nThe controller shall be listed by: Underwriters Laboratories, Inc., in accordance\nwith UL508A, Standard for Industrial Controls.\n3.\nThe controller shall be approved by: Factory Mutual (IEC 62091).\n\nD.\n\nController: UL listed, soft start fire pump controller with automatic transfer switch, in\nNEMA 250 Types 2 and 12 enclosure, including the following:\n1.\nDisconnect Switch: Externally operable, quick break type.\n2.\nCircuit Breaker: Size to NFPA 20, minimum 100,000 amperes interrupting\ncapacity.\n\nFire Pump & Standpipe Replacement Project\nFIRE PUMPS\nBellevue Hospital - H Building\n21 30 00 - 6\n462 1st Ave, New York, NY 10016\nProject No. 26-2112-000\nIssued for 100% Construction Documents April 12, 2024\n\n3.\n4.\n5.","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770138624770}}
{"type":"message","id":"e2b2ab8e","parentId":"937a8872","timestamp":"2026-02-03T17:10:25.086Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01FZB11ai1beopyAgFz1AzKS","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ARCHITECTURAL                                                                                 MECHANICAL                                                                                        FP-109.00         FIRE PROTECTION BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK 5TH FLOOR PART PLANS\nA-001.00          ZONING & BUILDING ANALYSIS LEGEND(S), ABBREVIATIONS, NOTES                  M-001.00          MECHANICAL SYMBOLS, ABBREVIATIONS, SCHEDULES AND NOTES                          FP-110.00         FIRE PROTECTION BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK 6TH FLOOR PART PLANS                  ALTERNATE 1 : ANY SCOPE REQUIRED OR ASSOCIATED WITH THE                                                                                (H)\nA-002.00          BUILDING DEPT. NOTES, SAFETY NOTES, GENERAL NOTES                           M-101.00          MECHANICAL BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK CELLAR PART PLAN 1                           FP-111.00         FIRE PROTECTION BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK 7TH FLOOR PART PLANS                  REMOVAL AND INSTALLATION FOR STANDPIPE 1 IN THE NORTH STAIR                                            ADMINISTRATION (A)\nA-003.00          FIRESTOPPING NOTES, FIRESTOPPING DETAILS                                    M-102.00          MECHANICAL BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK CELLAR PART PLAN 2                           FP-112.00         FIRE PROTECTION BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK 8TH FLOOR PART PLANS                  SHALL BE PRICED SEPARATELY.                                                                            C&D BLDG.\nA-101.00          CELLAR NORTH PARTIAL REMOVAL PLAN                                           M-103.00          MECHANICAL BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK MEZZANINE PART PLANS                         FP-113.00         FIRE PROTECTION BUILDING H REMOVAL WORK 9TH FLOOR PAR